- op: discuss  # 10cf
  at: '2026-11-16T11:46:39Z'  # 10cf
  by: agent  # 10cf
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 10cf
  clock: 4  # 10cf
  nonce: 10cf  # 10cf
  message: "Fixed in PR #2200. Re-ran the filed repro: the init and deinit of two same-named types declared in two functions shared one id each on dev (init 15a05d39..., deinit 1340cad2...) and g's ids moved when f's type was deleted; now the four ids are distinct and g's stay put on deletion. The init / deinit of a function-local type hashes the enclosing function in its scope chain. swift-composable-architecture: 6 symbols moved by this fix alone, every one an init of a type inside a test function. NOT DONE: INV-fabih's wide statement still fails for five other same-name-sibling shapes (two blocks of one function, two getters, label-only overloads, two inits, two closures): filed with the Swift residual. The change moves stable ids, so it shipped in the stableid v14 -> v15 bump; the spec's history row lists the rule and the measured share. Repro record (both arms, commands and copied outputs): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/tracker/repros.md; per-package detail: pr2/STATUS.md; churn: pr2/final_measure.txt."  # 10cf
